{
  "schema": "jdewitt.vocab-remap-weights/1",
  "scope": "Vocabulary-row edit of a quantized artifact: storage fidelity and byte accounting only. No model is loaded, no logits or generations are read, and no behavioral claim is made; the weight side of this card is gated for claims.",
  "method": "The denial table is resolved against the artifact tokenizer (the same byte-level BPE as --list, both contexts) and the resulting ids name rows of the token-embedding matrix and, when it is untied, of the output head. For each covered row W_i the edit is the rank-1 projection a refusal axis gets, with the axis being the row's own direction u = W_i/||W_i|| on the row's input side: dW_i = -s (W_i u^T) u = -s W_i, so the algebra and a per-row down-weight scale (1 - s) are the same operation and the same helper (ggufio.axis_delta) computes it. Rows outside the table are not touched by the edit. The write reuses ggufio.edit_tensors: every untouched tensor is copied byte for byte and the edited tensors are requantized at their own stored type, which keeps every tensor offset and byte length, so the revert sidecar can hold the pre-edit bytes and restore the artifact exactly. The dry run measures the edited blocks only (ggufio.preview_edit rows=) because the edit exists at a few dozen rows of a 151,936-row matrix; --apply re-measures the shipped bytes (ggufio.compare_edit rows=) against the pristine source. No model, no logits, no generation, and no behavioral claim: the weight side is measured here for storage fidelity only.",
